/-!
# B-line IL, pre-tables (B5), part 2: the register file and the basic steps

The pre-table programs keep their values in the registers `rg` (one integer each) and write
their outputs onto stacks outside `rg`. The managed state is `RF v c`: register `j ∈ rg` holds
`[v j]`, every other stack `j` holds `c j`.

* congruence of expressions: `eval`, `ok`, `cost`, `Bnd` only see the tops of the registers read;
* `spA` (assignment to a register of `rg`), `spU` (push onto a stack outside `rg`), `spO` (pop);
* `enC d eN eK eJ` / `epC d eN eK eJ eS`: `v d := expNeg n k j` / `expPos n k j σ` through the
  library programs `expNegP` / `expPosP` (inputs on `16, 17, 18, 27`, output on `19`).
-/

